nly guard (only the script claims both paths and HALTs on reuse). Carry the literal `RUN` and `RP` values into steps 7–9, since each Bash call is a fresh shell; the agent will write its report there and mark `$RP.done`. Otherwise (cmux / unpinned) leave `<REPORT_FILE_PATH>` empty and rely on the sentinel scrape. Measured on `audit-cycle-verb`: across the 18 impl-plan audit passes, 17 delivered via the report file (file present, non-empty, `.done` written); 1 did not — cycle 7 pass 1 wrote neither the report file nor the marker, and its report w [... truncated (1031 chars total)]"},{"line_number":2848,"content":"7. Stage: `cat > /tmp/audit_<feature>_<phase>_cycle<N>_run$RUN.txt`."},{"line_number":2855,"content":"   P=/tmp/audit_<feature>_<phase>_cycle<N>_run$RUN.txt"},{"line_number":2888,"content":"   hmad-dispatch send agy /tmp/audit_<feature>_<phase>_cycle<N>_run$RUN.txt"},{"line_number":2973,"content":"## Second surface — the codex leg"},{"line_number":2980,"content":"RP=/tmp/audit_<feature>_<phase>_cycle<N>_codex_run$RUN.report.md"},{"line_number":2985,"content":"  --out /tmp/audit_<feature>_<phase>_cycle<N>_codex_run$RUN.txt"},{"line_number":2999,"content":"hmad-dispatch exec codex /tmp/audit_<feature>_<phase>_cycle<N>_codex_run$RUN.txt \\"},{"line_number":3001,"content":"  --out /tmp/audit_<feature>_<phase>_cycle<N>_codex_run$RUN.out.txt \\"},{"line_number":3002,"content":"  --log /tmp/audit_<feature>_<phase>_cycle<N>_codex_run$RUN.log --timeout 1800"},{"line_number":3009,"content":"COLLECT_OUT=$(hmad-dispatch collect-report --surface codex \\"},{"line_number":3011,"content":"  --report \"$RP\" --out /tmp/audit_<feature>_<phase>_cycle<N>_codex_run$RUN.out.txt \\"},{"line_number":3059,"content":"it, then read it back before you route on it — `available` (or absent) routes to §\"Second surface —"},{"line_number":3067,"content":"RP=/tmp/audit_<feature>_<phase>_cycle<N>_teammate_run$RUN.report.md"},{"line_number":3072,"content":"  --out /tmp/audit_<feature>_<phase>_cycle<N>_teammate_run$RUN.txt"},{"line_number":3086,"content":"  \"PROMPT=/tmp/audit_<feature>_<phase>_cycle<N>_teammate_run$RUN.txt"},{"line_number":3101,"content":"COLLECT_OUT=$(hmad-dispatch collect-report --surface teammate \\"},{"line_number":3103,"content":"  --report \"$RP\" --out /tmp/audit_<feature>_<phase>_cycle<N>_teammate_run$RUN.out.txt \\"},{"line_number":3181,"content":"- `h_mad_collect_report.py` — collect-report surface collector: copies a delivered report-file or `--out` fallback into the docs audit path (the fallback reads a pane scrape past the dispatch boundary and an `exec` `--out` file from its end — see §6.6; conflating the two made it dead for `exec`), prints `COLLECT: OK|MISSING|CONFLICT` plus the collected path/delivery source, and performs readback before reporting success. `OK`/`MISSING`/`CONFLICT` exit 0 because they are measured outcomes; operational errors and readback failures exit 2. `--force` overwrites an existing collected report after a conflict."}]}]},"locations":[]}
{"type":"thought","data":"The SKILL.md has evolved"}
{"type":"thought","data":" past its original design."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe design's 6.6 literal"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is stale against the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" current SKILL.md. The"}
{"type":"thought","data":" effort contract requires"}
{"type":"thought","data":" reading the tree before"}
{"type":"thought","data":" asserting its contents."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The design incorrectly"}
{"type":"thought","data":" claims the SKILL.md"}
{"type":"thought","data":" path `RP=/tmp/audit_<feature>_<phase>_cycle<N>.report.md`,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" but this does not match"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the actual file."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe actual path includes"}
{"type":"thought","data":" a `_run$RUN` suffix."}
{"type":"thought","data":" This is a false claim"}
{"type":"thought","data":" about the tree. A 5e"}
{"type":"thought","data":" implementer writing"}
{"type":"thought","data":" tests today would write"}
{"type":"thought","data":" a regex that does not"}
{"type":"thought","data":" match. The question"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is whether this finding"}
{"type":"thought","data":" should be must-fix."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nAC-3.5a requires the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" 6.6 literal to be asserted"}
{"type":"thought","data":" against TRANSPORT_RE."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The design's wrong "}
{"type":"thought","data":"literal blocks implementers"}
{"type":"thought","data":" from matching the real"}
{"type":"thought","data":" staged name. They would"}
{"type":"thought","data":" either fail the test"}
{"type":"thought","data":" or hardcode the stale"}
{"type":"thought","data":" string and bypass the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" regex requirement."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe stale literal "}
{"type":"thought","data":"is a must-fix. It blocks the AC-3.5a test from"}
{"type":"thought","data":" being written as specified,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and if forced to match,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" it would pin a phantom"}
{"type":"thought","data":" filename that no longer"}
{"type":"thought","data":" exists.\n\nThe real staged"}
{"type":"thought","data":" name still satisfies"}
{"type":"thought","data":" TRANSPORT_RE because"}
{"type":"thought","data":" its stem contains no"}
{"type":"thought","data":" dots."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe grammar still "}
{"type":"thought","data":"matches the new filename."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The design's test cites"}
{"type":"thought","data":" a literal that is not"}
{"type":"thought","data":" staged, so it fails"}
{"type":"thought","data":" to lock the live recipe."}
{"type":"thought","data":" This gap is must-fix"}
{"type":"thought","data":" because AC-3.5a enforces"}
{"type":"thought","data":" what gets staged. The"}
{"type":"thought","data":" design also specifies"}
{"type":"thought","data":" that `gate()` should"}
{"type":"thought","data":" be inserted immediately"}
{"type":"thought","data":" after the `--verify-stamp`"}
{"type":"thought","data":" branch and before `read_text`."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe current main()"}
{"type":"thought","data":" contains round_cap "}
{"type":"thought","data":"and exit_check branches"}
{"type":"thought","data":" before verify_stamp."}
{"type":"thought","data":" These early returns"}
{"type":"thought","data":" do not read the audit"}
{"type":"thought","data":" file for scoring, so"}
{"type":"thought","data":" they do not affect "}
{"type":"thought","data":"the gate verdict. The"}
{"type":"thought","data":" design's placement "}
{"type":"thought","data":"of gate() immediately"}
{"type":"thought","data":" after verify_stamp "}
{"type":"thought","data":"and before read_text"}
{"type":"thought","data":" remains correct relative"}
{"type":"thought","data":" to the current code."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe design's placement"}
{"type":"thought","data":" of `gate()` immediately"}
{"type":"thought","data":" after `--verify-stamp`"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is correct. Early returns"}
{"type":"thought","data":" such as `--round-cap`"}
{"type":"thought","data":" skip the transport "}
{"type":"thought","data":"check entirely, so they"}
{"type":"thought","data":" do not interfere with"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the gate verdict. This"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is a should-fix at "}
{"type":"thought","data":"most.\n\nI also verified"}
{"type":"thought","data":" that `gate()` only "}
{"type":"thought","data":"accepts return codes"}
{"type":"thought","data":" 0 and 2."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe design code block"}
{"type":"thought","data":" `return 1` contradicts"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the specification. "}
{"type":"thought","data":"AC-3.1 requires exit"}
{"type":"thought","data":" 2, and AC-3.3 requires"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the gate verdict tuple"}
{"type":"thought","data":" that depends on exit"}
{"type":"thought","data":" 2. A return of 1 raises"}
{"type":"thought","data":" OperationalError instead"}
{"type":"thought","data":" of returning the required"}
{"type":"thought","data":" tuple. This is a must-fix"}
{"type":"thought","data":" restatement and contradiction."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe design also claims"}
{"type":"thought","data":" exactly two markers"}
{"type":"thought","data":" should be created, "}
{"type":"thought","data":"but the specification"}
{"type":"thought","data":" requires exactly one"}
{"type":"thought","data":" marker. This restates"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the requirement incorrectly"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and creates an internal"}
{"type":"thought","data":" contradiction."}
